Kaigi is the FreeGateway Project's privacy-hardened fork of MiroTalk SFU.
It provides self-hosted WebRTC conferencing with local browser assets,
per-user meeting grants, local or LDAP authentication, and no participant
presenter authority. The native mediasoup API and worker are supplied by
the www/mediasoup port.

Kaigi uses its own service, configuration, runtime and log directories so
that the independently maintained MiroTalk port can coexist.
